The description states that applying the operation to any object as both inputs gives that object back (an identity property). The assumption is that for any x, applying the operation to x and x yields x. The question asks whether applying the operation to x and y (Value 1) is always equal to applying it to y and x (Value 2).

The assumption translates to:
\boxed{op(x, x) = x}

The question translates to:
\boxed{op(x, y) = op(y, x)}
